  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "e93a97af-3a8e-48f5-8da5-fdcfc6729a08",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## Untitled workflow\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow processes meeting recordings by transcribing them, analyzing the content, and extracting action items.\nIt prepares CRM data, updates contact information in HubSpot, and creates tasks for action items.\nThe workflow drafts and sends emails to meeting attendees and saves a summary to Google Docs.\nFinally, it notifies the team via Slack about the completed tasks.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- [ ] Configure the webhook trigger for 'Meeting Recording Upload' to receive meeting recordings.\n- [ ] Set up credentials for Whisper API in the 'Transcribe with Whisper' node.\n- [ ] Configure HubSpot credentials for updating contacts and creating tasks.\n- [ ] Set up Gmail credentials for drafting and sending emails to attendees.\n- [ ] Configure Google Docs credentials for saving meeting summaries.\n- [ ] Set up Slack credentials for notifying the team.\n- [ ] Define the required configuration values in 'Workflow Configuration' (e.g., Whisper API URL, HubSpot contact email, Slack channel).\n\n### Customization\n\nCustomize the AI prompts in the 'Meeting Analyzer', 'Action Item Formatter', and 'Email Drafter' agents to match your specific requirements for meeting analysis and email drafting."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "da1c5d25-030d-4b14-89a9-54cb6559b147",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
